{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, err, give me one moment, this screen is hanging again. What brings you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): It's nothing much, doctor. Only some ringing in the right ear.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ringing. Sorry, which ear, say that again?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Right side only. Left one is fine.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): From how long?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm, three weeks... no, actually from one month, right ear only. I didn't think it was worth coming.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. All through the day?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): More when everything is quiet. At the workshop I hardly even notice. Not a big thing.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Workshop, meaning?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): I run a small fabrication unit. Grinding, power press, those loud machines the whole day.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): You wear ear plugs or muffs?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): No ear plugs, never used them. It is only noise, I am used to it.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any muffled hearing, sound a bit dull?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Slightly only, uh, right side. Like it is a bit blocked. Nothing serious.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is the ear paining?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really. No pain.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any discharge?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Dizziness?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): One second, file has come up. It says hypertension. You are on treatment, yes?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, BP only, from many years. It is under control, no need to go into all that.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, I scrolled past. The nurse has entered amlodapine five mg once daily. Is that right?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No, doctor. I take amlodipine 10 mg, once in the morning. Five mg was long back. Her entry is wrong.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ok. Any headache with the BP?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes, if I skip the tablet. Not every day.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): And chest pain?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Nurse has put today's pressure as one oh nine over seventy-seven. Last time, in March, you were one-forty over eighty-eight.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): See, today it is normal only. I told you BP is not the issue.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Temperature thirty-six point eight... no, sorry, thirty-six point four. Pulse seventy-four. Weight seventy-two kilograms.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Hmm. Fine.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me look in the right ear. Drum is intact, no redness, and I don't see any wax.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): I knew it would be nothing.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): My working impression is noise-related tinnitus from those machines, but I won't call it final until the hearing is tested.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): A test for this small ringing? I can manage, honestly.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): I am still referring you for pure tone audiometry. It will get booked.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Wait, right ear, yes? Sorry, a pop-up came.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes, right ear only. I already told you.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Please use ear plugs on those machines. And don't skip the amlodipine. Come back in three weeks with the report. If the ringing suddenly becomes much worse, or you get spinning, come earlier, don't wait."
 ],
